<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts, citing a soft Federal funds rate, had said the Fed was likely to stay out of the open market.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent at the Fed's typical time for open market operations. The Fed's target for the rate is 5-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
